    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. If λ ∈/ σ(D|J ) the resolvent R = (D − λI|J )−1 has the form Rx = ℓ(x)φλ + V (I − λV )−1x, with ℓ a continuous linear functional on C∞(D). Since Wϕ(λ) = 0 it follows that ϕλ(x) = ϕ(V (I − λV )−1x) = ϕ(Rx) = 0, for all x ∈ J . By the form of ϕ it follows easily that ϕλ has order N − 1 if N > 0. Moreover, Wϕλ(z) = ϕ(V (I − λV )−1φz)# = ϕ((z − λ)−1(φz − φλ))# = Wϕ(z) z − λ"
