    "bounding box" : [ 226.32, 332.176, 368.999, 349.461 ],
    "font" : "CMTI10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "J = {p(D)J : p polynomial}."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 27,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 81.6, 273.016, 513.729, 327.381 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. If σ(D|J ) = ∅ we have (D − λ)J = J for all λ and the equality in the statement holds. Conversely, if the equality holds, then (D − λI)J = J for each λ. Suppose for a contradiction that D − λ0I is not injective for some λ0. Then for each j ≥ 0 there exists a nonzero xj ∈ J , such that (D − λ0)jxj = φλ"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 29,
    "level" : "1",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 186.72, 277.837, 318.412, 292.61 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : ". From this it follows that Vλj"
  }, {
